ui-use-checkboxes-for-related-choices-that-can-be-selected-independently-a-parent-control-mak = Use checkboxes for related choices that can be selected independently. A parent control makes selecting many children easier.

ui-a-checkbox-contains-a-container-and-a-selection-icon = A checkbox contains a container and a selection icon.

ui-at-wider-breakpoints-a-contained-region-can-group-related-choices-and-actions = At wider breakpoints, a contained region can group related choices and actions.

ui-select-children-independently-the-parent-is-mixed-when-only-some-children-are-selected-sel = Select children independently. The parent is mixed when only some children are selected. Selecting a mixed parent selects every child; clearing it clears them all.

ui-use-a-switch-for-an-independent-binary-setting-that-takes-effect-immediately-use-radio-but = Use a switch for an independent binary setting that takes effect immediately. Use radio buttons for one choice from a set, checkboxes for related multiple choices, and buttons for commands.

ui-the-track-contains-a-handle-and-an-optional-icon-icons-should-communicate-on-or-off-clearl = The track contains a handle and an optional icon. Icons should communicate on or off clearly, such as a checkmark and a cross.

ui-settings-commonly-use-vertically-stacked-rows-with-an-inline-label-for-each-switch = Settings commonly use vertically stacked rows with an inline label for each switch.

ui-the-handle-moves-to-the-opposite-side-and-changes-size-as-the-value-changes-the-setting-ta = The handle moves to the opposite side and changes size as the value changes. The setting takes effect without a separate Save action.

ui-people-using-assistive-technology-need-to-find-the-control-change-its-selection-and-receiv = People using assistive technology need to find the control, change its selection and receive feedback about the result.

ui-both-the-label-and-checkbox-select-the-option-child-selections-remain-independent-a-partia = Both the label and checkbox select the option. Child selections remain independent; a partially selected parent reports a mixed state.

ui-touch-and-pointer-feedback-communicate-that-the-handle-is-interactive-keep-the-current-on = Touch and pointer feedback communicate that the handle is interactive. Keep the current on or off value easy to distinguish.

ui-keep-default-targets-at-least-48-by-48dp-a-denser-presentation-should-be-an-explicit-prefe = Keep default targets at least 48 by 48dp. A denser presentation should be an explicit preference that remains easy to reverse.

ui-focus-lands-on-the-switch-handle-space-or-enter-changes-its-value = Focus lands on the switch handle. Space or Enter changes its value.

ui-use-the-controls-below-to-try-keyboard-navigation = Use the controls below to try keyboard navigation.

ui-use-a-concise-label-that-describes-the-setting-an-accessible-name-should-clarify-ambiguous = Use a concise label that describes the setting. An accessible name should clarify ambiguous visible wording.

ui-choose-multiple-related-options-use-concise-labels-and-make-selected-unselected-and-mixed = Choose multiple related options. Use concise labels and make selected, unselected and mixed states easy to scan.

ui-turn-an-independent-setting-on-or-off-its-effect-is-immediate-and-the-handle-makes-the-cur = Turn an independent setting on or off. Its effect is immediate, and the handle makes the current value clear.

ui-alternate-selection-controls = Alternate selection controls

ui-checkboxes-allow-several-related-choices-radio-buttons-select-one-option-and-switches-cont = Checkboxes allow several related choices, radio buttons select one option, and switches control independent settings.

ui-retain-the-default-minimum-48dp-targets-let-people-explicitly-opt-into-a-denser-presentati = Retain the default minimum 48dp targets. Let people explicitly opt into a denser presentation.

ui-move-focus-between-enabled-controls = Move focus between enabled controls

ui-toggle-the-focused-control = Toggle the focused control
